# CakePHP MCP

Prefer `docs/index.md` and the `mcp-development` skill. **Alpha** — APIs may change.

@scoped(['config/mcp.php'])
## MCP config
- Register web/local servers and transports here (`Mcp.Servers` / `Mcp.local`) after bake.
- Keep OAuth / middleware settings aligned with Tessera docs when enabling remote auth.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Mcp/Servers/**', 'src/Mcp/Tools/**', 'src/Mcp/Prompts/**', 'src/Mcp/Resources/**'])
## MCP primitives
- Bake via `mcp_server` / `mcp_tool` / `mcp_prompt` / `mcp_resource` / `mcp_app_resource`.
- Wire classes on the server `$tools` / `$prompts` / `$resources` arrays.
- Tools need `schema` + `handle`; use `shouldRegister()` for conditional exposure; prefer `Response::*` factories.
@endscoped

@scoped(['templates/Mcp/**', 'templates/**/mcp/**'])
## MCP app templates
- Keep AppResource templates in sync with the baked PHP class; follow Apps docs for `ui://` resources.
@endscoped

@scoped(['tests/**'])
## MCP tests
- Prefer server test helpers / inspector over inventing fake MCP transports.
@endscoped
